Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:39:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: the colour of the film fits its row, and light
 levels not given say so
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The colour of the film (hades.video.color) had one line on the overview
(330 px for the value) and on the video page (410 px). The samples it was
measured with were all "BT.2020 · PQ · limited range", but a film in SDR
says "BT.709 · BT.709/BT.1886 · limited range" (418 px in English), and
one whose stream does not tag its colour more: Kodi takes the primaries by
the size of the picture, "BT.601 (PAL) (assumed) · BT.709/BT.1886 ·
limited range" (594 px; 611 px in Spanish). It was cut on both pages, in
English too.

The colour now takes two lines on both pages (HadesPanelRowText), which
gets the flash of a changed value as the other rows have it (on the video
page). The film column of the video page is as high as its rows can be
(a Dolby Vision film with HDR10+: the heading, 15 rows and the colour,
706 px, within the panel of 900).

The light levels of the film (hades.src.cll) are "none" where the video
gives MaxCLL and MaxFALL as 0: the video page showed "none nits" in every
language. They now say "not given" (#31834), as those sent to the display
already did (HadesSrcCllVar, as HadesOutCllVar). system/hades is made
again by make-playerinfo.py.

Host test (outside the tree): measure_all.py with the widest colour in
each language and light levels not given: 3 controls that do not fit
before in en_gb, es_es, es_ar and es_mx, none after. t_none.py (every
place that shows the light levels tests them for "none" first): 3 faults
before, none after.
